{"title":"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #5</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #3</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35df5f1800eac426739f20cae1ff726bc9fbedf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 cm$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2a0e3b70b9f69840f207631cb35ffc43e27bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{The length of a full size school bus} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{The height of a picnic table} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{The height of an elephant} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{The length of your foot} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{The length of your thumb}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1306\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using logic, we can conclude that the closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm is the length of your thumb. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/7/5979448a479ffa80bab0d763b12bcd3004bff890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"41\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CE